    "The CT06 extinction curve decreases monotonically from 1 to 5 $\\mu$m -- that part is correct. But \"decreasing extinction with wavelength\" means F360M (3.6 $\\mu$m, shorter wavelength) is extinguished **more** than F480M (4.8 $\\mu$m, longer wavelength), not less. As $A_V$ increases, F360M dims by more magnitudes than F480M does, so F360M$-$F480M **increases** -- that is the standard, expected reddening direction (same sense as F162M$-$F210M reddening in the other panel), not bluer.\n",
